ced-generation pedigrees of hybrid poplar</article-title><source>Canadian Journal of Forest Research</source><year>2005</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>1779</fpage><lpage>1789</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1139/x05-101</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>El-Lithy</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Clerkx</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruys</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Koornneef</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vreugdenhil</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quantitative Trait Locus Analysis of Growth-Related Traits in a New Arabidopsis Recombinant Inbred Population</article-title><source>Plant Physiology</source><year>2004</year><volume>135</volume><fpage>444</fpage><lpage>458</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15122039</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1104/pp.103.036822</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frary</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fritz</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanksley</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A comparative study of the genetic bases of natural variation in tomato leaf, sepal, and petal morphology</article-title><source>Theoretical and Applied Genetics</source><year>2004</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>523</fpage><lpage>533</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15150691</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00122-004-1669-x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Perez-Perez</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Serrano-Cartagena</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Micol</surna